WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.615
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, I think we’re all here. Morning everyone! How’s everyone doing today?

2
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.037
Kwame Asante: Hey! Doing well, thanks. Coffee’s finally kicking in.

3
00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:18.302
Hannah Weiss: Hi all! I’m good, just got back from a quick walk. It’s actually sunny for once.

4
00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:24.630
Tomás Rivera: Morning. I’m here, just finishing up a call with Legal, but I’m all yours now.

5
00:00:24.844 --> 00:00:30.998
Grace Liu: Hi everyone! I’m good, just juggling a couple onboarding calls this week, but nothing too wild.

6
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.276
Sofia Lindqvist: Glad to hear it. Anything urgent before we jump in?

7
00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:40.818
Kwame Asante: Nope, just the usual onboarding questions in Slack, but nothing major.

8
00:00:41.954 --> 00:00:45.800
Hannah Weiss: Same here, just prepping for the next absence management training.

9
00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:58.174
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, let’s get to the main item. We need to review the eligibility for becoming an onboarding buddy. There’s been some feedback that the three-month requirement is a bit restrictive.

10
00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:06.283
Grace Liu: Yeah, I’ve heard that too. Some folks feel ready after two months, especially if they’ve onboarded quickly themselves.

11
00:01:07.381 --> 00:01:15.073
Kwame Asante: I’ve had a couple people ask if they can start sooner, especially in smaller teams where we need more buddies.

12
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:23.420
Tomás Rivera: From a legal perspective, I don’t see any risk in shortening the eligibility, as long as managers still approve.

13
00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:32.720
Hannah Weiss: I think as long as the manager signs off, two months should be fine. Most people are up to speed by then.

14
00:01:33.951 --> 00:01:39.335
Sofia Lindqvist: So, are we leaning toward changing the eligibility from three months to two months?

15
00:01:39.656 --> 00:01:43.887
Kwame Asante: I’d support that. It’ll help us fill the buddy pool faster.

16
00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:50.144
Grace Liu: Agreed. And it gives new hires a chance to get involved sooner, which is motivating.

17
00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.744
Tomás Rivera: No objections here.

18
00:01:53.342 --> 00:01:55.265
Hannah Weiss: Sounds good to me too.

19
00:01:56.221 --> 00:02:05.067
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, let’s make it official: we’ll update the policy so team members are eligible to be onboarding buddies after two months, not three.

20
00:02:05.882 --> 00:02:11.651
Kwame Asante: Got it. I’ll update the handbook page and the onboarding issue template to reflect that.

21
00:02:12.542 --> 00:02:16.772
Sofia Lindqvist: Thanks, Kwame. Can you aim to have that done by Friday?

22
00:02:17.526 --> 00:02:21.372
Kwame Asante: Yep, Friday works. I’ll ping you all when it’s live.

23
00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:24.041
Grace Liu: Great, thanks Kwame.

24
00:02:24.671 --> 00:02:31.210
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, moving on—quick note on the engagement survey results. Participation was up this quarter, which is awesome.

25
00:02:32.324 --> 00:02:35.785
Hannah Weiss: That’s great! Do we know what drove the increase?

26
00:02:36.337 --> 00:02:44.414
Sofia Lindqvist: Mostly the reminders in Slack and the new incentives. I’ll share the full breakdown in the People Ops channel later today.

27
00:02:44.941 --> 00:02:48.403
Tomás Rivera: Nice, always good to see more feedback coming in.

28
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.760
Grace Liu: Do we have a plan for sharing the results with the broader team?

29
00:02:54.210 --> 00:03:02.671
Sofia Lindqvist: Yes, I’ll draft a summary post for the #company-announcements channel. Kwame, can you help pull out a couple key stats for that?

30
00:03:03.027 --> 00:03:07.258
Kwame Asante: Sure thing, I’ll get those to you by end of day.

31
00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.654
Hannah Weiss: Thanks, both!

32
00:03:10.845 --> 00:03:13.153
Sofia Lindqvist: Anything else before we wrap up?

33
00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.093
Tomás Rivera: Nothing from me.

34
00:03:15.575 --> 00:03:17.075
Grace Liu: All good here.

35
00:03:17.904 --> 00:03:19.404
Kwame Asante: Nope, I’m set.

36
00:03:20.546 --> 00:03:22.046
Hannah Weiss: I’m good too.

37
00:03:23.516 --> 00:03:30.439
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, thanks everyone. Kwame, let us know when the handbook’s updated. Have a great rest of your day!

38
00:03:31.321 --> 00:03:32.859
Kwame Asante: Will do. Bye all!

39
00:03:33.427 --> 00:03:34.927
Grace Liu: Bye!

40
00:03:35.258 --> 00:03:36.758
Tomás Rivera: Take care, everyone.

41
00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.710
Hannah Weiss: Bye!

42
00:03:39.206 --> 00:03:40.706
Sofia Lindqvist: Bye, thanks again.

43
00:03:41.139 --> 00:03:46.524
Kwame Asante: Oh, quick note—I’ll also update the FAQ doc since it mentions the three-month thing.

44
00:03:46.742 --> 00:03:48.242
Sofia Lindqvist: Good catch, thanks!

45
00:03:49.137 --> 00:03:50.637
Grace Liu: Appreciate it, Kwame.

46
00:03:51.193 --> 00:03:52.693
Tomás Rivera: Thanks, Kwame.

47
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.660
Hannah Weiss: Thanks!

48
00:03:56.579 --> 00:03:59.272
Kwame Asante: No problem. Have a good one, everyone.

49
00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:04.224
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, closing the call now. See you all next week.
